  "published": "2026-11-17T07:59:42.183Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Usernameless passkey sign-in (discoverable credentials), as a mode of its own beside the WebAuthn second factor: WebAuthnOptionsGenerator.CreateDiscoverableRegistrationOptions and CreateDiscoverableAuthenticationOptions, and WebAuthnVerifier.VerifyDiscoverableRegistration and VerifyDiscoverableAuthentication, which checks the assertion's user handle against the credential owner's, after the signature. User verification is always required in this mode. WebAuthnAuthenticationResult gains Mode (SecondFactor or Discoverable), and WebAuthnAuthenticationFailureReason gains UserHandleMissing and UserHandleMismatch. The second-factor methods keep their signatures and behaviour; only the message of the empty allow-list refusal changed, to point at the passkey method. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-v5.15.0/EasyReasy.Auth/README.md#migration-from-5140",
